                <pb facs="0181" n="161" xml:id="pg161"/>

                <head><seg type="margin">[644]</seg> *<hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hunter, Acting
                        Secretary of State, to Mr. Dickinson, district attorney.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1866-01-25"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 25,
                        1866</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">D. S. Dickinson</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >United States Attorney, New York:</hi></p>
                <p>Your telegram of yesterday readied here too late in the evening to be then
                    answered. At present no suggestions or instructions from this Department
                    relative to the case of the Météor are deemed necessary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
